Resume a paused sandbox (POST /v2/sandboxes/{id}/connect). A running
sandbox is left running; its timeout is only ever extended.

When the server has no capacity yet (a host is starting, or the sandbox
server is waking), a resume waits up to --capacity-wait (10 minutes by
default) and prints a progress line on stderr each time it retries.

Usage:
  anona-compute resume SANDBOX_ID [flags]

Flags:
      --capacity-wait duration   how long a resume waits while the server has no capacity yet, e.g. a host is starting (0 = do not wait; env ANONA_COMPUTE_CAPACITY_WAIT) (default 10m0s)
  -h, --help                     help for resume
      --timeout string           sandbox lifetime from now (default "300s")

Global Flags:
      --api-key string             API key (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_KEY, E2B_API_KEY)
      --api-url string             API URL (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_URL, E2B_API_URL; default https://api.<E2B_DOMAIN>)
      --json                       JSON output on stdout (same as -o json)
  -o, --output string              output format: text or json (default "text")
      --profile string             config profile to use (env ANONA_COMPUTE_PROFILE; default "default")
      --request-timeout duration   timeout for each API request (0 = none)
  -v, --verbose                    verbose output on stderr
